## 1. Executive summary

A frontend quality-assurance layer has been established following a standard test pyramid, with clear separation between unit/component testing, network simulation, and end-to-end verification of the critical journey. The browser is treated as an untrusted client; UI guards are therefore never a substitute for API authorization.

The verification stack is aligned with a risk-based, layered test strategy consistent with the process intent of ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119 and ISTQB guidance, with accessibility smoke checks inspired by WCAG 2.2 through automated axe rules. The current baseline protects session handling, routing guards, HTTP orchestration, and the login surface. Depth on domain CRUD flows remains planned work.

**Baseline verdict:** fit as a quality foundation. It is suitable for gating CI on the shared critical modules, but it is not yet a product-wide regression suite. The enforced coverage figure applies only to a deliberately scoped set of modules and must not be quoted as project-wide coverage.

