## 6. Test strategy

### 6.1 Principles

1. **Risk-based:** prioritize session handling, auth client logic, routing guards, and HTTP error handling over decorative UI.
2. **Behavior over implementation:** query by role, label, and text; drive the UI with `userEvent`.
3. **Single network fake:** MSW only. Never mock Axios or `fetch` ad hoc in feature tests.
4. **Pyramid:** many fast unit and component tests; few E2E flows.
5. **Defense-in-depth awareness:** UI tests make no claim of authorization coverage.

### 6.2 Test levels

```text
                 ┌─────────────────────┐
                 │  E2E (Playwright)   │  Critical journeys only
                 │  Chromium/FF/WebKit │
                 └──────────▲──────────┘
                            │
                 ┌──────────┴──────────┐
                 │ Client integration  │  useApi + MSW handlers
                 │ (MSW)               │
                 └──────────▲──────────┘
                            │
         ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐
         │ Component + a11y (RTL, jest-axe)    │
         └──────────────────▲──────────────────┘
                            │
         ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐
         │ Unit (pure utils / validators)      │
         └─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

| Level | Tooling | Typical items |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unit | Vitest | `auth`, `safeUrl`, `financeMetrics`, `carImageValidation` |
| Component | Vitest + RTL + user-event | `Toggle`, `ProtectedRoute` |
| Client integration | Vitest + MSW | `useApi` success and validation error |
| Accessibility smoke | jest-axe | Selected controls |
| E2E | Playwright | Login form rendering and sign-in journeys: successful login, wrong password, non-admin account, and unauthenticated redirect under `/dashboard/login` |
| Static | ESLint, `tsc --noEmit` | Hygiene checks |

### 6.3 Design techniques in use

| Technique | Application |
| --- | --- |
| Equivalence partitioning | Opaque tokens vs JWT vs missing tokens |
| Boundary values | Image size at maximum bytes ± 1 |
| Decision tables (lightweight) | Auth expiry rules |
| Negative testing | MSW 422 validation payloads |
| Accessibility tree assertions | `getByRole` and `getByLabel` |
| Exploratory (manual, complementary) | Pre-release RTL/LTR and CRUD smoke (not automated) |

