## 9. Metrics and coverage policy

### 9.1 Structural coverage

- **Provider:** V8
- **Reporters:** text, html, lcov
- **Thresholds:** 70% lines, 70% functions
- **Gated surface (`include`):** shared utils, `useApi`, selected components (`Toggle`, `ProtectedRoute`), and feature utils already under test
- **Global report:** coverage across all of `src/` is generated alongside, with no threshold, so the true project-wide figure is always visible. The enforced percentage applies to the gated surface only and must never be quoted as project coverage.

**Rationale:** gating the entire `src/features/**/pages` tree at 70% before tests exist would produce a permanently failing CI. The include list is an intentional quality perimeter, expanded feature by feature.

### 9.2 Product metrics (recommended tracking)

| Metric | Source | Target direction |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Defect escape rate (production bugs lacking a test) | Issue tracker | Decreasing |
| Flaky E2E rate | CI run history | Low and trending down |
| Time to fix a broken main branch | CI and issue tracker | Under one business day |
| Critical flows with E2E | Test inventory | Growing (sign-in success and failure, non-admin account, and unauthenticated redirect are now included; logout and one CRUD flow remain planned) |

### 9.3 Flaky-test policy

A test that fails intermittently is fixed or quarantined with a tracking issue within one sprint. CI retries are a diagnostic aid, not a fix, and a quarantined test must have an owner.

